      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Microinjection of neurotensin into the rat rostroventromedial medulla produces dose-dependent inhibition of the tailflick reflex (ED50 of 2.06 nmol/animal (1.33-3.19)). The peak effect occurs 15-20 min following injection and, at the highest dose used, lasts up to 70 min."},
